Verify cloud-init completion via guest status after boot scripts finish.

First-boot progress monitoring can stall after boot.sh logs
"Exiting with code 0" and writes /run/lima-boot-done (#782):
- cloud-init-main.service units using Type=oneshot + RemainAfterExit=yes
  emit "Finished cloud-init-main.service" without deactivating or logging
  a "Consumed ... CPU time" line, and units without CPU accounting may
  deactivate without a Consumed line.
- The /var/log/cloud-init-output.log awk fallback advanced the start line
  on any line after "Cloud-init ... finished", causing trailing lines to
  skip the current boot's completion line.
- Emitting the Running status event overwrote currentStatus instead of
  atomically preserving CloudInitProgress.

This patch recognizes "Finished cloud-init-main.service", fixes the awk
start-line filter to advance only on a new "Cloud-init ... running" line
after an earlier completion, serializes status updates under eventEncMu,
and adds an authoritative post-boot guest status probe that triggers only
after finalRequirements confirms /run/lima-boot-done matches the current
boot (preserving #828's safeguard against premature completion).

